is not included.

Modifications made for the CHGame port (2026):

  * Rewritten for the CHGame handheld (CH32X035 RISC-V, 128x128 ST7735 colour
    LCD, piezo) on the CHGfx library instead of Arduboy2/ArdBitmap/Sprites.
  * Re-laid out from 128x64 to 128x128: the dealer stands behind the table,
    cards are 22x28 (PPOT's width and 12 px overlap), bet circle, chip rack,
    shoe and printed felt.
  * All art in colour: PPOT's dealer (recoloured, then retouched by hand in
    tools/art/common/dealer.png), suit glyphs, title logo, splash logo and win/lose
    lettering; new card ranks, pips, court-card portraits, chips, and new
    dealer expressions.
  * Game logic separated from rendering (Round.cpp keeps PPOT's
    ViewState flow) and covered by host unit tests.
  * Rules: casino preset (six-deck shoe, dealer stands on all 17s, peeks on
    ace and ten, blackjack beats 21) with a "Classic" preset keeping PPOT's
    rules.
  * Bugs fixed: insurance paid 1:1 and partial insurance paid nothing (now
    2:1); a button press during the result highlight could credit a win
    twice; no bankruptcy check after a peek loss; over-insuring on $1 bets;
    a blackjack was not auto-stood.
  * New: card deal/flip/re-centre animation, chip flights and payouts,
    rolling purse, particles, banners, screen shake, palette effects,
    talking/blinking dealer, sound effects and music, LED effects, options,
    statistics (with a reset), saved games, pause menu, an attract-mode demo
    and a credits page thanking Press Play On Tape.
